          "_label": "Details (Official List Description)"
        }
      ],
      "content": "LITTLE GADDESDEN       \tLITTLE GADDESDEN SP 9913  \t\t\t\t\t(East side)                                        9/194 -                                      \t\tNo. 49 GV                                       \tII House. C17 or earlier, cased in red brick in C18/C19, N gable chimney and small NE extension in 1870's for Lord Brownlow, S wing added in 1930's after sale of estate and buttresses to front wall are probably of this time. Timber frame cased in red brick, brick S wing, old red tile roofs. A 2-storeys house, the older part has 2 flush 3-light Yorkshire sliding casement windows with small panes to each floor, and a 2-light window in the place of the former central door. Heavy brick buttresses with 2 offsets between the openings. Sun Fire Insurance plaque no. 209530 on wall (for policy of June 1764 to Thomas Groome, carpenter) and large external N gable chimney with white brick quoins and red brick tumbled offsets. White brick dressings and decorative vent holes to N lean-to extension set back to centre of chimney. Higher 2 storeys S wing has 2 storeys canted bay window to right of entrance. A 3 bay timber frame with original roof. (Senar(1983)96). Listing NGR: SP9956513025"
    }
  ],
